      'Eben Thurston is a search marketing executive based in the New York ' +
      'City metropolitan area who has worked in digital marketing and search ' +
      'for over 20 years. He was most recently Director, Integrated Search at ' +
      'TIAA (January 2024 to May 2026), and has held search leadership roles ' +
      'at iQuanti, ' +
      'FULLBEAUTY Brands, Fareportal, Shutterstock and Time Inc. He holds an ' +
      'MBA from Fordham University.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is Eben Thurston working on now?',
    a:
      'He works as an independent advisor on search and AI visibility, ' +
      'helping brands adapt as discovery shifts from ranked links to ' +
      'generated answers. His current engagement is Purely Mat Pilates, a ' +
      'boutique studio in Westchester County, where he leads customer ' +
      'acquisition and built the site himself with Claude Code. He also ' +
      'writes about generative engine optimization at ebenthurston.com.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What kind of role is Eben Thurston looking for?',
    a:
      'Senior in-house leadership at a large brand, owning search marketing, ' +
      'AI search and GEO, or broader digital growth. He is most effective in ' +
      'regulated and high-consideration categories, particularly financial ' +
      'services, insurance and financial media, where compliance constraints ' +
      'and long buying cycles make search a governance problem as much as a ' +
      'performance one. He also takes selective advisory engagements.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What did Eben Thurston do at TIAA?',
    a:
      'As Director, Integrated Search from January 2024 to May 2026, he ' +
      'directed organic, paid and AI search across the TIAA and Nuveen ' +
      'brands, managing the paid search program and directing SEO and SEM ' +
      'teams at four agencies alongside product marketing, editorial, media, ' +
      'engineering and compliance. His focus was the move to AI search: he ' +
      'built the measurement layer for AI-referred traffic before standard ' +
      'tooling existed, and over the following year AI Overview appearances ' +
      'across the two brands grew from 2.6K to 20.5K while organic clicks ' +
      'held flat against an industry-wide decline in click-through rates.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does a GEO win actually look like?',
    a:
      'One concrete example: TIAA holds position one in organic results for ' +
      '"lifetime income", a competitive non-branded term in a regulated ' +
      'category, and the same page is cited as a source in Google AI ' +
      'Overviews for that query. Anyone can run the search and check. That ' +
      'pairing demonstrates the mechanism most GEO advice only asserts, which ' +
      'is that AI citations overwhelmingly come from pages that already rank. ' +
      'The position was established during his tenure and has held since.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is Generative Engine Optimization (GEO)?',
    a:
      'Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) is the practice of earning ' +
      'visibility and citations for a brand inside generative AI systems such ' +
      'as ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini and Google AI Overviews. Where ' +
      'classic SEO optimizes for ranked links, GEO optimizes for being ' +
      'retrieved, trusted and quoted in synthesized answers. Answer Engine ' +
      'Optimization (AEO) is used interchangeably, with success measured in ' +
      'mention rate rather than rankings and clicks.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do GEO and AEO fit into modern search marketing?',
    a:
      'They are extensions of search marketing, not replacements for it. SEO ' +
      'drives traffic through ranked links, SEM captures paid demand, and AEO ' +
      'ensures a brand is accurately retrieved and cited inside AI-generated ' +
      'answers. The underlying assets overlap heavily (entity clarity, ' +
      'authoritative content, clean technical foundations), which is why ' +
      'running them as one commercial engine works better than as separate ' +
      'teams with separate goals.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do regulated brands earn visibility in AI answers?',
    a:
      'Regulated brands win AI visibility the same way they win regulatory ' +
      'trust: verifiable, compliance-approved claims published in ' +
      'machine-readable form. That means pre-rendered HTML that AI crawlers ' +
      'can actually read, structured data that removes ambiguity about the ' +
      'entity making each claim, fact-dense content mapped to real user ' +
      'prompts, and review workflows that keep every extractable statement ' +
      'inside approved language. Constraint, handled well, becomes a citation ' +
      'advantage: answer engines favor precise, attributable sources.',
  },
];

// JSON-LD knowledge graph. One @graph, four nodes, cross-referenced by @id.
const schema = {
