---

<Base title="Eben Thurston | SEO, SEM & AI Search Executive | Ex-TIAA" description={description}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} slot="head" />

  <div class="hero">
    <div>
      <h1>Eben Thurston</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Eben Thurston has worked in digital marketing and search for over 20
        years.
      </p>
      <p class="lede">
        He was most recently Director, Integrated Search at TIAA, a Fortune 100
        financial services firm, where he directed organic, paid and AI search
        across TIAA and Nuveen against a single set of goals. He now advises
        independently on search and AI visibility.
      </p>
    </div>
    <img
      class="headshot"
      src="/eben-thurston.jpg"
      alt="Eben Thurston, search marketing executive based in New York"
      width="576"
      height="576"
      loading="eager"
    />
  </div>

  <h2 id="key-facts">Key Facts</h2>
  <p>
    Search leadership across financial services, marketplaces, ecommerce and
    media. At TIAA he managed roughly $10M in annual paid search spend against
    96.4M organic impressions, directed SEO and SEM teams at four agencies, and
    worked across a matrix spanning product marketing, editorial, media,
    engineering and compliance.
  </p>
  <p>Selected results:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>TIAA holds position one organically for "lifetime income" and the same page is cited in Google's AI Overview for that query</li>
    <li>AI Overview appearances 2.6K to 20.5K across TIAA and Nuveen (Q4 2025 versus the same quarter a year earlier)</li>
    <li>Traffic referred from AI platforms up 479%, to 8,833 sessions (same period)</li>
    <li>Held organic clicks flat through a 32% industry-wide CTR decline</li>
    <li>Organic impressions up 43%, to 96.4M</li>
    <li>Performance Max at 30% of IRA account conversions on 25% of spend, 18% better cost per acquisition than account average</li>
    <li>Search was the top-producing channel through Shutterstock's $170M to $425M run, across 20+ languages and territories</li>
    <li>Led a 20-person team across New York and India for a top-four US bank</li>
    <li>Two client properties acquired, by <a href="https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/webmd-acquires-additude-301299280.html">WebMD</a> and Recurrent Ventures</li>
    <li>Started as a front-end developer at Time Inc.</li>
    <li>Played <a href="https://www.sports-reference.com/cbb/players/eben-thurston-1.html">Division I basketball</a> at the University of Vermont</li>
    <li>Built and shipped <a href="https://purelymatpilates.com">purelymatpilates.com</a> and five browser games with AI coding tools</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="cv">CV</h2>

  <h3>Independent Advisor, Search &amp; AI Visibility <span class="meta">(November 2025 to present)</span></h3>
  <p>
    Eben advises on search and AI visibility for brands working through the
    shift from ranked links to generated answers. Current engagement: Purely Mat
    Pilates, where he leads customer acquisition and digital growth for a
    boutique studio in Westchester County. He built and launched
    <a href="https://purelymatpilates.com">purelymatpilates.com</a> with Claude
    Code, covering technical SEO, page speed and schema architecture, and the
    rebuild is documented in
    <a href="/insights/geo-on-a-local-business-site/">GEO on a Local Business Site</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>Director, Integrated Search, TIAA <span class="meta">(January 2024 to May 2026)</span></h3>
  <p>
    Eben Thurston directed organic, paid and AI search across TIAA and Nuveen,
    at a Fortune 100 financial services firm competing with Fidelity, Vanguard
    and Schwab for the same demand. He managed roughly $10M in annual paid
    search spend against 96.4M organic impressions, directed SEO and SEM teams
    at four agencies, and worked across a matrix spanning product marketing,
    editorial, media, engineering and compliance.
  </p>
  <p>
    His focus was the shift to AI search. He built the measurement layer for
    AI-referred traffic before standard tooling existed, then aligned product
    marketing, editorial and media against what it showed. Through a year in
    which organic click-through rates fell about a third industry-wide, the two
    brands held clicks flat while impressions grew, and he shifted spend from
    paid to organic on terms where rankings were already strong.
  </p>
  
  <h3>Director, Search Marketing, iQuanti <span class="meta">(2021 to 2023)</span></h3>
  <p>
    He led search strategy and delivery for iQuanti's enterprise financial
    services portfolio, running a 20-person team across New York and India on
    the agency's largest account, a top-four US bank, and beating its traffic
    and performance targets. He held the full enterprise portfolio through the
    2023 banking-sector volatility with zero churn, moved client reporting from
    traffic metrics to revenue attribution, and built review workflows across
    SEO, Legal and Compliance that raised speed to production in regulated
    environments.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Authored original research on Google SGE, measuring the overlap between its top-three citations and the top-three organic ranking pages, one of the first attempts to quantify the relationship between ranking and AI citation</li>
    <li>Co-authored the firm's position paper on using ChatGPT for SEO content, arguing against replacing content teams with AI</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Director, Digital Marketing / Director, SEO, FULLBEAUTY Brands <span class="meta">(2017 to 2020)</span></h3>
  <p>
    Across three years at FULLBEAUTY Brands, Eben co-led digital marketing for a
    12+ brand portfolio, first as Director of SEO and then as Director of
    Digital Marketing, driving 30% year-over-year organic growth and 80% growth
    in total demand. He owned the organic search P&amp;L, directed 18 site
    migrations including eight to Salesforce Commerce Cloud, and led marketing
    and technical alignment through M&amp;A integrations.
  </p>

  <h3>Director, SEO &amp; Content Strategy, Fareportal <span class="meta">(2016 to 2017)</span></h3>
  <p>
    He recovered and stabilized organic search for a global travel
    marketplace carrying legacy algorithmic penalties. He built the governance
    framework, compliance protocols and risk-mitigation playbooks that
    rehabilitated domain authority and held it through subsequent algorithm
    updates, moving search from a reactive cleanup function to a governance
    pillar.
  </p>

  <h3>SEO Product Owner, Global, Shutterstock <span class="meta">(2012 to 2016)</span></h3>
  <p>
    Eben owned organic search as the top-producing marketing channel through
    Shutterstock's run from $170M to $425M in revenue, across 20+ languages and
    territories, and ran a $30M paid media program alongside it. He diagnosed a
    crawl and indexation defect that unlocked a 300% increase in non-English
    traffic, consolidated the Footage subdomain from page two to top three
    rankings, and embedded discoverability requirements into engineering
    sprints.
  </p>

  <h3>Founder &amp; Managing Director, Spring Marketing Strategies <span class="meta">(2009 to 2012)</span></h3>
  <p>
    He founded and scaled a digital consultancy, managing the full
    P&amp;L and service delivery for 30+ retainer clients including Time Inc. He
    architected audience development for BobVila.com, later acquired by
    Recurrent Ventures, and established ADDitude Magazine as the primary digital
    authority for neurodiversity, later
    <a href="https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/webmd-acquires-additude-301299280.html">acquired by WebMD</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>Earlier roles</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Director, Marketing &amp; Audience Development at 1-800-FLOWERS.COM / Celebrations.com, where organic traffic grew 267% in four months.</li>
    <li>Managing Director, Digital Marketing at Root Markets, a mortgage lead exchange co-founded by <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lewis_Ranieri">Lewis Ranieri</a>, operating at the intersection of Wall Street securitization and digital customer acquisition.</li>
    <li>Time Inc., across web production, front-end development, web analytics, and business development, negotiating content and technology partnerships with Google, Facebook, and Yahoo.</li>
    <li>Wall Street foundations at Morgan Stanley, Lehman Brothers, and Goldman Sachs.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Education</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>MBA, <a href="https://www.fordham.edu/gabelli-school-of-business/">Fordham University, Graduate School of Business Administration (Gabelli School)</a> (Marketing; Product Management).</li>
    <li>BA, Political Science &amp; English, University of Vermont, where he played Division I basketball.</li>
  </ul>

